claims:
1. A method of measuring semantic relevance of keywords by parsing information resources, comprising:
receiving, by a data processing system having one or more processors, from a content provider computing device corresponding to a domain entity having a web address, a seed keyword to generate additional keywords relevant to the seed keyword;
accessing, by the data processing system, a semantic relationship graph including a plurality of nodes and a plurality of edges, each of the plurality of nodes referencing at least one corresponding keyword, each of the plurality of edges connecting a corresponding pair of the plurality of nodes and defining a corresponding semantic distance between a pair of at least one keywords referenced by the pair of the plurality of nodes;
identifying, by the data processing system, using semantic relationship graph, a plurality of keyword categories including a first keyword category and a second keyword category, each of the plurality of keyword categories including a plurality of keywords, each of the plurality of keywords having a semantic distance from the seed keyword less than a semantic distance threshold as defined by a corresponding plurality of edges in the semantic relationship graph;
retrieving, by the data processing system, an information resource of the domain entity using the web address, the information resource having primary content;
determining, by the data processing system, for each keyword of the first keyword category and the second keyword category, a frequency of the keyword occurring with the seed keyword on the primary content of the information resource of the domain entity retrieved using the web address;
generating, by the data processing system, for each keyword of the first keyword category and the second keyword category, a keyword-seed affinity score based on the frequency of the keyword occurring with the seed keyword on the primary content of the information resource of the domain entity identified using the web address;
determining, by the data processing system, for the first keyword category, a first category-seed affinity score based on the keyword-seed affinity scores for each of the plurality of keywords in the first keyword category;
determining, by the data processing system, for the second keyword category, a second category-seed affinity score based on the keyword-seed affinity scores for each of the plurality of keywords in the second keyword category;
identifying, by the data processing system, a semantic conflict between the first keyword category and the second keyword category based on the semantic distance between at least one of the plurality of keywords in the first keyword category and at least one of the plurality of keywords in the second keyword category as defined by a corresponding edge within the semantic graph;
comparing, by the data processing system, responsive to identifying the semantic conflict between the first keyword category and the second keyword category, the first category-seed affinity score to the second category-affinity score;
determining, by the data processing system, based on the comparison, that the first category-seed affinity score is greater than the second category-seed affinity score; and
transmitting, by the data processing system, to the content provider computing device for display, the plurality of keywords of the first keyword category and the plurality of keywords of the second keyword category, the plurality of keywords in the first keyword category indicated as selected responsive to determining that the first category-seed affinity score is greater than the second category-seed affinity score, the plurality of keywords in the second keyword category indicated as unselected responsive to determining that the second category-seed affinity score is less than the first category-seed affinity score.

2. The method of claim 1, further comprising:
identifying, by the data processing system, using the semantic relationship graph, the semantic conflict among the first keyword category, the second keyword category, and a third keyword category;
determining, by the data processing system, based on the semantic conflict, a first category group and a second category group, the first category group including the first keyword category, the second category group including the second keyword category and the third keyword category;
determining, by the data processing system, a first group-seed affinity score for the first category group and a second group-seed affinity score for the second category group; and
comparing, by the data processing system, the first group-seed affinity score to the second group-seed affinity score; and
wherein transmitting for display the plurality of keywords further comprises transmitting the plurality of keywords, the first keyword category indicated as selected and the second keyword category and the third keyword category indicated as unselected responsive to determining that the first group-seed affinity score is greater than the second group-seed affinity score.

8. The method of claim 1, further comprising;
identifying, by the data processing system, using the semantic relationship graph, from the plurality of keywords, a first topical keyword representative of the first keyword category and a second topical keyword representative of the second keyword category, the first topical keyword having a first minimum semantic distance from each of the plurality of keywords in the first keyword category less than the semantic distance threshold, the second topical keyword having a second minimum semantic distance from each of the plurality of keywords in the second keyword category less than the semantic distance threshold; and
wherein transmitting for display the plurality of keywords further comprises transmitting for display the plurality of keywords categorized into the first keyword category with the first topical keyword and the second keyword category and with the second topical keyword, responsive to identifying the first topical keyword and the second topical keyword.

