15. A method of measuring semantic relevance of keywords by parsing information resources, comprising:
receiving, by a data processing system having one or more processors, from a content provider computing device corresponding to a domain entity having a web address, a seed keyword to generate additional keywords semantically relevant to the seed keyword;
accessing, by the data processing system, from a database, a semantic relationship graph including a plurality of nodes representing keywords and a plurality of edges, each of the plurality of edges connecting two respective nodes of the plurality of nodes and defining a semantic distance between the two keywords representing the two respective nodes, at least one of the plurality of edges indicating that the two keywords represented by the respective nodes of the plurality nodes as semantically conflicting;
traversing, by the data processing system, the plurality of nodes of the semantic relationship graph to identify a seed node representing the seed keyword and for each of the candidate nodes adjacent to the seed node a semantic distance between the seed keyword and the keyword of the adjacent node as defined by a corresponding plurality of edges in the semantic relationship graph;
identifying, by the data processing system, a set of candidate nodes from the plurality of nodes adjacent to the seed node having a respective edge with a respective semantic distance between a seed node-candidate node pair of less than a semantic distance threshold;
retrieving, by the data processing system, a plurality of information resources of the domain entity using the web address, each information resource of the plurality of information resources having primary content;
parsing, by the data processing system, for each candidate keyword of the set of candidate nodes, the plurality of information resources to determine a frequency at which the seed keyword and the candidate keyword occur across the primary content of the plurality of the information resources retrieved using the web address of the domain name;
identifying, by the data processing system, from the candidate keywords of the set of candidate nodes, a first set of keywords corresponding to a first subset of the set of candidate nodes and a second set of keywords corresponding to a second subset of the set of candidate nodes;
identifying, by the data processing system, a semantic conflict between at least one of a first set of candidate keywords and at least one of a second set of candidate keywords based on the respective edge of the semantic relationship graph indicating two corresponding keywords as semantically conflicting;
comparing, by the data processing system, a first frequency of at least one of the first set of candidate keywords to a second frequency of at least one of the second set of candidate keywords, responsive to identifying the semantic conflict; and
transmitting, by the data processing system, to the content provider computing device, instructions to display at the content provider computing device, the first set of keywords as selected as relevant and the second set of keywords as unselected as irrelevant based on the comparison.

16. The method of claim 15, further comprising:
computing, by the data processing system, for each candidate keyword of the set of candidate keyword, a normalization factor based on a frequency at which the respective keyword occurs in a general corpus different from the plurality of information resources;
adjusting, by the data processing system, for each candidate keyword of the set of candidate keyword, the frequency by the normalization factor for the respective keyword.
